      "message": "ci(browser): require the no-new-privs argument in the R7L invariant\n\nThe R7L static-invariant step pinned the launcher token\n'set_no_new_privs()', the bare call form that cannot compile against\nthe workflow's own sha256-pinned rustix 1.1.4 (signature:\nset_no_new_privs(no_new_privs: bool) -> io::Result<()>, prctl.rs:631).\nRun 33214554916 failed at this token after the compile repair supplied\nthe required argument, proving the token encoded the defect rather\nthan the invariant.\n\nRequiring 'set_no_new_privs(true)' pins the actual semantic (NNP\nenabled) and is strictly stronger: it also rejects a future regression\nto set_no_new_privs(false), which the old token accepted.\n\nEvidence: E0061 at src/bin/a2-skill-source-launcher.rs:31 against the\nlocked dependency set (Cargo.lock ffdf4d85... verified unchanged by the\nsame workflow's dependency-closure step).\n\nAuthored-by: GLM 5.3 (zai/glm-5.3) - R7L CI repair, third slice.",
